# A FIXED DEFECT, named after it (Go's `test/fixedbugs`).
#
# SYMPTOM (2026-08-13, found by M-program-corpus at its second step, writing the
# JSON reader's `Json` variant): `heroes check` HUNG. Forever, one core at 100%,
# no output and no exit — on a variant with a case named `null` and any case in
# it carrying a payload. Not a wrong diagnostic and not a crash. The first
# program of the milestone whose deliverable is programs met it in its first
# minute, which is the milestone working rather than slipping.
#
# CAUSE: `syntax/members.rs`'s `case_block` recovered from a refused case name
# with `skip_line`, and `skip_line` stops *before* an `Indent` by design — so the
# next line is parsed on its own merits instead of being swallowed. The refused
# case's payload block was therefore still under the cursor on the next turn of
# the loop, fell into the same `_` arm, and `skip_line` returned without moving.
# `field_block` next door has had an `Indent` arm since it was written; the case
# parser never did, and no case reached it because every test of a refused case
# name used a case with no payload.
#
# FIX: one arm, `cur.balanced_block()`, which drops the orphaned block. Silently,
# because `recover.rs`'s rule is that one bad declaration costs one diagnostic
# and the case name already spent it — the reader is told about `null`, not about
# the two lines that were a consequence of it.
#
# `nullptr` is the repair the message names, and the last declaration is the
# CONTROL: a case with a payload, read rather than dropped. A recovery that
# started eating good blocks would pass this file's first half and fail here.
# Bulk regression case.

variant Json
    null                        #~ reserved_word
        text: str
    number
        v: i64

variant Reference
    absent
    present
        target: i64

function main()
    print(1)
